---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import AgenticNav from "../../components/AgenticNav.astro";
import cases from "../../../public/agentic-le/cases.json";
import run from "../../../public/agentic-le/replay/live-exemplar.json";
const modelResponses = run.events.filter(e => e.kind === "request").length;
const artifacts = run.events.filter(e => e.kind === "artifact").length;
---
<Base title="Agentic LE · Capability Matters"
 description="From a seed idea to a runnable candidate product, with public agent discussion, scenario challenges, evidence and versioned artifacts.">
 <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
 <AgenticNav active="cases" />
 <header class="intro container-wide">
  <p class="eyebrow">Agentic learning engineering · Problems → Products</p>
  <h1>Teams at work. Every case, with its work shown.</h1>
  <p>A learning engineer orchestrates specialist agents from a seed idea to a candidate product. Explore the discussion, challenges, revisions and code for each project.</p>
 </header>
 <section class="container-wide lab">
  <section id="cases" aria-labelledby="cases-heading">
   <h2 id="cases-heading">Explore all {cases.cases.length} live-agent cases</h2>
   <p class="case-note">Real agent execution on fictional problems. Human pilot approval and field evidence remain pending.</p>
   <div class="case-grid">{cases.cases.map(c => <article class="case-card" id={`case-${c.id}`}>
    <p class="case-domain">{c.label.replace(" · live agents", "")}</p>
    <h3>{c.title}</h3>
    <p class="case-counts">{c.counts.request} model calls · {c.counts.artifact} artifact versions · {c.counts.scenario} scenario challenges</p>
    <nav class="case-actions" aria-label={c.title}>
     <a class="replay-link" href={`/agentic-le/replay/?case=${c.id}&v=case-demos-3`}>Replay this case</a>
     <a href={c.product}>Try its candidate</a>
     <a href={`${c.product}product.zip`} download>Download record & product</a>
    </nav>
   </article>)}</div>
   <p class="source"><a href="/agentic-le/record/?file=%2Fagentic-le%2Fcases.json">Case inventory and journal hashes</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/blob/main/docs/lifecycle/CASES.md">Expansion checklist</a></p>
  </section>
  <p class="paper-link"><a href="/agentic-le/paper/"><strong>Read the working paper: Learning Engineering in Action</strong></a></p>
  <div class="grid">
   <article><h2>Inside the workforce candidate</h2><p><strong>{run.seed.title}</strong> helps a new team lead rehearse a fictional feedback decision, consider another explanation, revise an approach and recover from an interruption. Its reflection is descriptive; it does not assess employees.</p><p>The handoff contains executable HTML, requirements, versioned artifacts, the project journal and a source-linked manifest. It is a candidate product requiring affected-person review and field validation.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/record/?file=%2Fagentic-le%2Fproduct%2Fmanifest.json">Inspect the product handoff</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/product/requirements.md">Read the requirements</a></p></article>
   <article><h2>Inside the workforce record</h2><p>The saved fictional workforce project contains {modelResponses} real model responses, including a rejected correction, and {artifacts} artifact versions. Scenarios changed interruption privacy and reviewer-conflict requirements. An actual missing-code finding reopened Build.</p><p>The replay preserves original drafts, dissent, prompts, provider metadata, failed validation and the corrected candidate. Recorded browser checks support only the behavior exercised in that environment.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/record/?file=%2Fagentic-le%2Freplay%2Flive-exemplar.json">Inspect the source journal</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/replay/?v=case-demos-3">Follow the workforce revisions</a></p></article>
  </div>
  <article><h2>Reusable roles and proficiency targets</h2><p>Roles inherit a common contribution contract, then specialize by discipline and relevant domain. They reference the five LENS competency domains. Requested proficiency describes the contribution expected in a simulation; demonstrated proficiency requires separately reviewed task evidence.</p><p>The existing exemplar used earlier fixed prompts. Its history is preserved without retrospectively assigning these new targets. Future runs pin the resolved role profiles and their versions in the journal.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/roles/">Explore roles, inheritance and evidence requirements</a></p></article>
  <article><h2>From candidate to operational product</h2><p>Understand → Map → Design → Build → Instrument → Deploy → Evaluate → Refine is a revisitable cycle. Build produces the executable candidate; refinement can return to any invalidated requirement. The learning engineer integrates the work and keeps human and system requirements visible.</p><p>Real use needs accountable ownership, affected-person review, appropriate data handling, accessible operation, a meaningful comparison and stopping rules. Learning, workplace transfer and flourishing remain claims to investigate. Inadequate conditions can justify changing the product, changing the work system, or stopping.</p><p>The hosted site serves saved products and replay. New model runs use the local runner in this repository; hosted model access and a shared job queue remain future work.</p></article>
  <p class="source"><a href="/problems-to-prototypes/">Return to project seeds</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/tools/lifecycle">Runner source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/docs/lifecycle">Specification and operating documentation</a></p>
 </section>
</Base>
<style>
 #cases{scroll-margin-top:7rem}.intro{padding-top:1.4rem;padding-bottom:1rem}.intro .eyebrow{margin-bottom:.6rem}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem);margin-bottom:.45rem}.intro p:last-child{max-width:52rem;margin-bottom:0}.lab{padding-top:.6rem;padding-bottom:3rem}.case-note{max-width:none;color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.case-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.case-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;background:var(--tint);padding:1.15rem}.case-domain{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:.7rem}.case-card h3{font-size:1.3rem;min-height:2.4em}.case-counts{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}.case-actions{display:grid;gap:.45rem;margin-top:auto;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem}.case-actions a{width:fit-content}.case-actions .replay-link{background:var(--ink);color:white;padding:.45rem .75rem;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:.2rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.4rem}article{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.4rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem;background:var(--bg)}h2{font-size:1.4rem;margin-top:0}.source{font-size:.85rem;max-width:none}.paper-link{margin:1.6rem 0}.lab a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent-2);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.case-grid,.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.case-card h3{min-height:0}.case-card{margin-bottom:0}.case-grid{margin-bottom:1rem}}
</style>
